THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
====================

AndrOsint does not include ADB or scrcpy. When the user asks for it, the
program downloads them from their official sources into the tools/ folder
next to it:

  - Android SDK Platform-Tools (ADB), by Google
    <https://developer.android.com/tools/releases/platform-tools>
  - scrcpy, by Genymobile, under the Apache License 2.0
    <https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy>

They are separate programs, not part of this one: each comes with its own
license terms, in the files downloaded with it.

AndrOsint uses the Python libraries CustomTkinter, Pillow, darkdetect and
packaging. The standalone executable built with scripts/build_exe.py also
contains Python and Tcl/Tk. Each of them remains under its own license.

